  'cashless-driving-licence-testing-centres-from-1-december-2026-11-24',
  'Sixteen Cape Town driving licence centres stop taking cash from 1 December',
  'Business', '2026-11-24', 'City of Cape Town', 'https://www.capetown.gov.za/media-and-news/sixteen-driving-licence-testing-centres-will-be-cashless-from-1-december/',
  'The City says 16 of its driving licence testing centres will accept only cashless payment from 1 December, after a pilot at three centres.',
  'The City of Cape Town has announced that sixteen of its driving licence testing centres will operate on a cashless basis from 1 December. Residents who plan to visit one of these centres should arrange a non-cash way to pay before they go.

According to the City, a pilot began on 1 October at three centres: Brackenfell, Fish Hoek and Strand. The City says the trial showed the benefits of a cashless system, and it is now adding 13 more centres. The City has not named those 13 centres in its announcement, so residents may want to check with their local centre.

The cashless approach covers traffic fine payments, learner and driver licence applications, licence card renewals or replacements, and Public Driving Permit applications. The City says two further centres, Joe Gqabi and Lingelethu West, will follow in 2027.

The City gives several reasons for the change. It says handling less cash lowers the risk of theft, reduces the reconciliation workload for staff and cuts cash collection fees. It also describes the move as part of its drive towards digital services. The announcement does not list which payment methods will be accepted.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.capetown.gov.za/media-and-news/sixteen-driving-licence-testing-centres-will-be-cashless-from-1-december/", "https://vocfm.co.za/16-cape-town-driving-licence-testing-centres-to-go-cashless-from-december/"]',
  'agent'
);
